.shell cmd

# deskhud-suite hotkeys (installed to ~/.config/whkdrc).
#
# Win is the window-manager key, so apps keep all their Alt and Ctrl shortcuts. Win combos not listed
# here still do what Windows does (Win+V, Win+Shift+S, Win+E...). Win+L cannot be taken over, so arrows
# replace the usual h/j/k/l.
#
# Lines starting with ## become sections in the hotkey list (bar keyboard icon, or Win+Shift+/).
# The keys are run by deskhud's keyboard hook (setting `keyboard.hook` in ~/.config/deskhud/settings.json),
# not by whkd: it reads this file in whkd's format and picks up edits when you save. With the hook off,
# deskhud ignores this file and GlazeWM's own `keybindings` apply instead.
#
# A line is `keys : command`. `deskhud <verb>` runs one of deskhud's commands, `glazewm command <cmd>`
# sends a GlazeWM command (https://github.com/glzr-io/glazewm#commands), anything else runs in cmd.

## Focus
win + left              : glazewm command focus --direction left
win + right             : glazewm command focus --direction right
win + up                : glazewm command focus --direction up
win + down              : glazewm command focus --direction down

## Move
win + shift + left      : glazewm command move --direction left
win + shift + right     : glazewm command move --direction right
win + shift + up        : glazewm command move --direction up
win + shift + down      : glazewm command move --direction down

## Stacks
# Win+T stacks the windows next to this one into tabs, or lays a stack out again (one button).
# Win+Alt+arrow stacks onto the window that way; on a stack, it pulls that window in.
win + t                 : glazewm command toggle-tabbed
win + alt + left        : deskhud stack left
win + alt + right       : deskhud stack right
win + alt + up          : deskhud stack up
win + alt + down        : deskhud stack down
win + oem_4             : glazewm command focus --prev-tab
win + oem_6             : glazewm command focus --next-tab
win + alt + back        : deskhud unstack

## Size and layout
win + ctrl + right      : glazewm command resize --width +3%
win + ctrl + left       : glazewm command resize --width -3%
win + ctrl + up         : glazewm command resize --height +3%
win + ctrl + down       : glazewm command resize --height -3%
win + z                 : deskhud snap
win + shift + z         : glazewm command toggle-tiling-direction

## Windows
win + q                 : glazewm command close
win + m                 : deskhud minimize
win + shift + m         : deskhud restore
win + ctrl + m          : deskhud tray next
win + f                 : glazewm command toggle-floating
win + shift + f         : glazewm command toggle-fullscreen

## Workspaces
# Numbers follow your screen: a number in use stays on its screen, and Win+N goes there; a free number
# opens on the screen you're on. Win+Shift+N takes the window along by the same rule. The numbers are
# the ones on the bar's left islands.
win + 1                 : deskhud workspace 1
win + 2                 : deskhud workspace 2
win + 3                 : deskhud workspace 3
win + 4                 : deskhud workspace 4
win + 5                 : deskhud workspace 5
win + 6                 : deskhud workspace 6
win + 7                 : deskhud workspace 7
win + 8                 : deskhud workspace 8
win + 9                 : deskhud workspace 9
win + shift + 1         : deskhud move-to-workspace 1
win + shift + 2         : deskhud move-to-workspace 2
win + shift + 3         : deskhud move-to-workspace 3
win + shift + 4         : deskhud move-to-workspace 4
win + shift + 5         : deskhud move-to-workspace 5
win + shift + 6         : deskhud move-to-workspace 6
win + shift + 7         : deskhud move-to-workspace 7
win + shift + 8         : deskhud move-to-workspace 8
win + shift + 9         : deskhud move-to-workspace 9

## Apps
# Focus the app if it is open anywhere, otherwise start it. Which app each name means is set
# under "apps" in ~/.config/deskhud/settings.json.
win + return            : deskhud open terminal
win + b                 : deskhud open browser
win + j                 : deskhud open ide
win + o                 : deskhud open notes

## Desktop
win + oem_2             : deskhud cheatsheet
win + shift + w         : deskhud wallpaper next
win + shift + p         : glazewm command wm-toggle-pause
win + shift + r         : glazewm command wm-redraw
win + shift + o         : glazewm command wm-reload-config
win + ctrl + shift + o  : deskhud reload
